#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:76
msgid "Hardening"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:80
msgid "Safe defaults: no code editor in wp-admin, no username discovery, no admin-level role for new accounts, generic login errors, no version disclosure, XML-RPC off and basic security headers. Adds a registration check to Site Health."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:87
msgid "Disable the theme/plugin file editor"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:91
msgid "Block username discovery"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:92
msgid "For visitors who are not logged in: ?author=N scans, the REST users endpoint, the users sitemap and author data in oEmbed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:96
msgid "Keep new accounts out of admin-level roles"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:97
msgid "If the default role for new accounts can manage users, plugins, options, the shop or raw HTML (for example after a database attack), new accounts get Subscriber instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:101
msgid "Generic login errors"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:102
msgid "One message for a wrong username or a wrong password, on wp-login.php and the WooCommerce login form."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:106
msgid "Hide the WordPress version"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:110
msgid "Reduce passive WordPress discovery"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:111
msgid "Remove REST API discovery links, RSD, Windows Live Writer and shortlinks from page metadata and headers. REST endpoints and asset versions keep working. Some publishing clients may need manual configuration; this does not hide WordPress from a determined scanner."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:115
msgid "Disable XML-RPC"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:116
msgid "xmlrpc.php answers 403. The WordPress mobile app and old desktop editors stop working with this site. Skipped automatically when Jetpack or WooPayments is active."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:120
msgid "Disable XML-RPC pingbacks"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:121
msgid "Remove pingback methods and the X-Pingback header, including when Jetpack or WooPayments needs authenticated XML-RPC. Other XML-RPC methods are unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:125
msgid "Basic security headers"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:126
msgid "X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy and X-Frame-Options (same origin). Pages served from a full-page cache may not get them."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:130
msgid "HSTS (1 year, this domain only)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:131
msgid "Only on HTTPS. Browsers will refuse plain HTTP for a year, so turn it on only when HTTPS works everywhere on this domain."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:212
msgid "Sorry, you are not allowed to list users."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:249
msgid "SafeHouse registration check"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:267
msgid "New accounts are set to get a role that can manage the site"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: role name, e.g. Administrator.
#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:270
#, php-format
msgid "The default role for new accounts is %s, which can manage users, plugins, settings or the shop, or post raw HTML. Attackers set this so that they can register their own administrator. Change it in Settings → General and check who changed it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:274
msgid "Until then SafeHouse gives new accounts the Subscriber role."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:278
msgid "Anyone can register an account"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: role name, e.g. Subscriber.
#: src/Modules/Hardening.php:281
#, php-format
msgid "The \"Anyone can register\" setting is on, with %s as the role for new accounts. Bots use open registration for spam accounts and to probe plugins that trust any logged-in user. If the site does not need WordPress accounts, turn it off in Settings → General. WooCommerce customer accounts have their own setting and keep working."
msgstr ""

