#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:64
msgid "LiteSpeed page cache"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:68
msgid "On LiteSpeed servers, pages for visitors who are not logged in and have no cart are served from the server cache without running WordPress. SafeHouse only sends cache headers and clears the cache after changes; it writes no files. Logged-in users, the cart, checkout and account pages are never cached."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:75
msgid "Keep pages for (minutes)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:76
msgid "At most 8 hours, so forms on cached pages still carry a valid security token. Changes clear the cache anyway."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:82
msgid "Never cache these paths"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:83
msgid "One per line, for example /contact/. A line matches every address that starts with it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:94
msgid "The LiteSpeed Cache plugin is active and manages the server cache itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:251
msgid "Clear the cache"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:257
msgid "LiteSpeed was asked to clear the cache."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:265
msgid "This server is LiteSpeed. Tools → Site Health checks whether it actually serves pages from its cache."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:266
msgid "This server does not look like LiteSpeed, so the cache headers have no effect here."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:270
msgid "Public caching is paused until the server checks personal cookies before serving cached pages. Ask your host to apply these rewrite rules to this site and restart LiteSpeed, then run the SafeHouse LiteSpeed test in Site Health. No files are changed automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:270
msgid "Verify an anonymous cache hit, then repeat with a WordPress login or WooCommerce cart cookie and without _lscache_vary: the response must not be a cache hit."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:280
msgid "SafeHouse LiteSpeed page cache"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:326
msgid "LiteSpeed served a cached page despite a personal cookie"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:327
msgid "Disable public caching and have your host correct the cookie vary rules, restart LiteSpeed and purge existing pages. Test each login, cart and password cookie without _lscache_vary before re-enabling caching."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:330
msgid "LiteSpeed serves pages from its cache"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:331
msgid "The home page came from cache for an anonymous visitor; each personal cookie separately bypassed that cached page without relying on the supplementary vary cookie."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:334
msgid "LiteSpeed public caching is paused until cookie rules are configured"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:335
msgid "Apply the cookie vary rewrite rules shown in the SafeHouse LiteSpeed settings, restart LiteSpeed and run this test again. PHP response headers alone do not protect sessions created before activation on OpenLiteSpeed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:338
msgid "LiteSpeed does not serve pages from its cache yet"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:339
msgid "The server is LiteSpeed, but the home page was not served from its cache. On LiteSpeed Enterprise add this to .htaccess, or ask your host to turn the cache on: <IfModule LiteSpeed> CacheLookup public on </IfModule>. A page that sets a cookie for every visitor is never cached either."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:342
msgid "The server is not LiteSpeed"
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:343
msgid "The LiteSpeed page cache module has no effect on this server. Switch it off, or use the cache your host provides."
msgstr ""

#: src/Modules/LiteSpeed.php:347
msgid "WooCommerce geolocates customers without page caching support, so cached pages may show one country's prices and taxes to everyone. In WooCommerce → Settings → General choose \"Geolocate (with page caching support)\"."
